    {
        "content": "<p>Hi, in Haskell <img alt=\":haskell:\" class=\"emoji\" src=\"https://avatars.zulip.com/3121/emoji/images/ee76e4c8.png\" title=\"haskell\"> you can write a normal function in infix form using backticks, like:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Haskell\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nf\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">`</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"p\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and you can use an infix operator as a normal function using parentheses:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Haskell\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>What is the Lean equivalent?</p>",
        "id": 594271868,
        "sender_full_name": "Serhii Khoma (srghma)",
        "timestamp": 1778500772
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 594272946,
        "sender_full_name": "Etienne Marion",
        "timestamp": 1778500999
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And for the first question, this works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 594273485,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1778501119
    }
]